<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>GRIFFIN Project Briefing -- Architecture & Direction</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --navy: #1a2332;
    --slate: #2d3748;
    --blue: #3182ce;
    --blue-light: #ebf4ff;
    --green: #276749;
    --green-light: #f0fff4;
    --orange: #c05621;
    --orange-light: #fffaf0;
    --red: #c53030;
    --red-light: #fff5f5;
    --purple: #6b46c1;
    --purple-light: #faf5ff;
    --teal: #2c7a7b;
    --teal-light: #e6fffa;
    --gray-50: #f7fafc;
    --gray-100: #edf2f7;
    --gray-200: #e2e8f0;
    --gray-300: #cbd5e0;
    --gray-500: #718096;
    --gray-600: #4a5568;
    --gray-700: #2d3748;
    --gray-800: #1a202c;
    --font-sans: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    --font-mono: 'Cascadia Code', 'Fira Code', 'Consolas', monospace;
  }

  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    color: var(--gray-800);
    line-height: 1.7;
    background: var(--gray-50);
  }

  /* === HEADER === */
  .hero {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--navy) 0%, var(--slate) 100%);
    color: white;
    padding: 3rem 2rem 2.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .hero .subtitle {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: #a0aec0;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .hero-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #cbd5e0;
  }
  .hero-meta span { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; }

  /* === NAVIGATION === */
  .toc {
    background: white;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    padding: 0.8rem 2rem;
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 10;
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .toc a {
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--gray-600);
    padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    transition: all 0.15s;
  }
  .toc a:hover { background: var(--blue-light); color: var(--blue); }

  /* === MAIN CONTENT === */
  .container {
    max-width: 960px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  /* === SECTIONS === */
  .section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  .section-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gray-200);
  }
  .section-number {
    background: var(--navy);
    color: white;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .section-header h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--gray-800);
  }

  /* === CARDS === */
  .card {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .card-blue { border-left: 4px solid var(--blue); }
  .card-green { border-left: 4px solid var(--green); }
  .card-orange { border-left: 4px solid var(--orange); }
  .card-red { border-left: 4px solid var(--red); }
  .card-purple { border-left: 4px solid var(--purple); }
  .card-teal { border-left: 4px solid var(--teal); }

  .card h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--gray-800);
  }
  .card p, .card li {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .card ul, .card ol {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .card li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }

  /* === STATS ROW === */
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .stat {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.25rem 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .stat-value {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--blue);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .stat-label {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--gray-500);
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }

  /* === DIAGRAMS === */
  .diagram-container {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .diagram-container h4 {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    color: var(--gray-500);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .diagram-container svg {
    display: block;
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* === TABLES === */
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  th {
    background: var(--gray-100);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gray-300);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.3px;
    color: var(--gray-600);
  }
  td {
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  tr:hover td { background: var(--gray-50); }

  /* === TAGS === */
  .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.3px;
  }
  .tag-done { background: #c6f6d5; color: #22543d; }
  .tag-progress { background: #fefcbf; color: #744210; }
  .tag-proposed { background: #e9d8fd; color: #44337a; }
  .tag-risk { background: #fed7d7; color: #742a2a; }
  .tag-question { background: #bee3f8; color: #2a4365; }

  /* === CALLOUT === */
  .callout {
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .callout-blue { background: var(--blue-light); border-left: 3px solid var(--blue); }
  .callout-green { background: var(--green-light); border-left: 3px solid var(--green); }
  .callout-orange { background: var(--orange-light); border-left: 3px solid var(--orange); }
  .callout-red { background: var(--red-light); border-left: 3px solid var(--red); }
  .callout-purple { background: var(--purple-light); border-left: 3px solid var(--purple); }
  .callout strong { font-weight: 700; }

  /* === CODE === */
  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    background: var(--gray-100);
    padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  .footer {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--gray-500);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  /* === RESPONSIVE === */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; }
    .hero-meta { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
    .stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .toc { padding: 0.5rem; }
    .toc a { font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem; }
  }

  @media print {
    .toc { position: static; }
    body { background: white; }
    .hero { padding: 1.5rem; }
    .section { page-break-inside: avoid; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- HEADER -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="hero">
  <h1>GRIFFIN Project Briefing</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">W&M HR Position Classification & Pay Matching Tool -- Architecture & Direction</p>
  <div class="hero-meta">
    <span>BUAD 5742 (AI) -- Poster April 15</span>
    <span>BUAD 5722 (Big Data) -- Deck April 17</span>
    <span>Client: Chas Ritinski, Total Rewards Manager, W&M HR</span>
    <span>Updated: March 30, 2026</span>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- TABLE OF CONTENTS -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<nav class="toc">
  <a href="#summary">Executive Summary</a>
  <a href="#mvp">MVP vs. Full Scope</a>
  <a href="#done">What's Done</a>
  <a href="#pipeline">Current Pipeline</a>
  <a href="#proposed">Proposed ML Integration</a>
  <a href="#data-strategy">Data Strategy</a>
  <a href="#course-mapping">Course Mapping</a>
  <a href="#questions">Questions for Professors</a>
  <a href="#risks">Risks & Mitigations</a>
  <a href="#timeline">Timeline</a>
</nav>

<div class="container">

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- 1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="section" id="summary">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-number">1</div>
    <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="callout callout-blue">
    <strong>The problem:</strong> William & Mary HR manually classifies staff positions into Virginia's DHRM taxonomy to determine career groups and pay bands. This is slow, subjective, and hard to audit. We're building a tool that automates this using AI + ML, producing transparent, explainable recommendations that HR can trust.
  </div>

  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-value">56</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Career Groups</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-value">294</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Roles Parsed</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-value">9</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Pay Bands</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-value">666</div>
      <div class="stat-label">SOC Codes</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-value">100%</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Coverage</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card card-green">
    <h3>Where We Are</h3>
    <p><strong>Workstream 1 (Data Collection) is complete.</strong> All 56 DHRM career group pages scraped, parsed (50 HTML + 6 PDF with 3 format variants), validated, loaded to SQLite, and exported as 7 Excel files. The FY26 salary structure, W&M pay grades (46 grades), and the DHRM-to-W&M crosswalk are built and validated (Band 7 -> S18 confirmed against the Assistant Controller example).</p>
    <p style="margin-top:0.5rem"><strong>Client engagement is active.</strong> Chas Ritinski (Total Rewards Manager, W&M HR) responded on March 27 directing us to use W&M's public Workday job board (~149 active postings) as real position descriptions for training and testing. Postings include pay bands, job profiles, and compensation grades we can use as ground truth labels. Approved AI tools at W&M: <strong>Copilot and Gemini</strong>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card card-purple">
    <h3>Where We're Heading</h3>
    <p><strong>We're proposing a hybrid ML + LLM architecture</strong> that goes beyond simple prompt-based classification. An H2O AutoML model would provide quantitative shortlisting and confidence scoring, while the LLM provides nuanced final classification with natural language explanation. When both systems agree, confidence is high. When they disagree, HR is flagged to apply human judgment. This design demonstrates course concepts from both classes and produces a more robust, trustworthy tool.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:0.75rem"><strong>New: AI Assignment 5 as Architecture Proof-of-Concept (PoC).</strong> Assignment 5 requires a LangChain multi-agent system with 8 components (agents, tools, memory, orchestration, streaming, etc.). We plan to <strong>integrate this directly into GRIFFIN</strong> as a formal milestone. Prof. Chung confirmed that LangChain is acceptable for production since it's open source -- so the LangChain multi-agent system IS the production architecture. The Streamlit app wraps LangChain agents directly, and LLM-agnostic design comes free via <code>init_chat_model()</code> (HR swaps between Gemini/Copilot/Claude by changing a config string). This satisfies Assignment 5, builds the production app, and meets the client's requirements in one effort.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- 2. MVP vs. FULL SCOPE -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="section" id="mvp">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-number">2</div>
    <h2>MVP vs. Full Scope: What We Promised vs. What We're Building</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="callout callout-red">
    <strong>Scope awareness:</strong> We added significant scope when we combined two course milestone projects (AI and Big Data) into one integrated system. The sections below describe the <em>full academic scope</em>. But the original commitment to our client is simpler, and that commitment comes first.
  </div>

  <div class="card card-green">
    <h3>MVP: What We Promised the Client (Minimum Viable Product)</h3>
    <p>We committed to delivering a tool similar to a <strong>Google Gemini Gem or a Claude Project</strong> -- a configured LLM workspace where HR can:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Paste a stale position description</strong> into the tool</li>
      <li>Receive a <strong>classification recommendation</strong> (up to 2 career group/role matches)</li>
      <li>Receive a <strong>compensation range recommendation</strong> (W&M salary grade, e.g., S15)</li>
      <li>Read the LLM's <strong>reasoning</strong> for why it chose that classification</li>
    </ol>
    <p style="margin-top:0.75rem">This is achievable with what we have <em>today</em>: our DHRM reference data (56 career groups, 294 roles, pay crosswalk) loaded as context into any LLM, plus the classification prompt template (v1). <strong>No ML model, no multi-agent system, no H2O required.</strong> If everything else falls through, the client still gets what they were promised.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card card-purple">
    <h3>Full Scope: What We're Building for Both Courses</h3>
    <p>On top of the MVP, we're building the hybrid ML + LLM architecture to demonstrate course concepts and produce a more robust, auditable tool:</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>What It Adds Beyond MVP</th><th>Course Value</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>H2O AutoML model</strong></td>
          <td>Quantitative shortlist with probabilities -- a second opinion independent of the LLM</td>
          <td>Big Data: AutoML, GBM, variable importance, SHAP, class imbalance</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Confidence scoring</strong></td>
          <td>ML + LLM agreement check -- HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW confidence flag</td>
          <td>Both: interpretability, trustworthy AI, audit trail</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>LangChain multi-agent system</strong></td>
          <td>Production backend + Assignment 5 deliverable (Prof. Chung confirmed open source is fine)</td>
          <td>AI: agentic design, multi-agent orchestration, tool use, memory</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Fairness guard</strong></td>
          <td>Flags potential bias in classifications across occupational families</td>
          <td>Both: responsible AI, ethics reflection</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>SHAP explanations</strong></td>
          <td>Per-classification waterfall showing which features drove the ML's recommendation</td>
          <td>Big Data: local + global interpretability</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="callout callout-green">
    <strong>The rule:</strong> MVP first, always. Every layer of the full scope is additive -- it makes the tool better, but the client's deliverable does not depend on it. If timeline pressure forces cuts, we cut from the bottom of the table up, never from the MVP.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- 3. WHAT'S DONE -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="section" id="done">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-number">3</div>
    <h2>What's Done (Workstream 1)</h2>
  </div>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Deliverable</th>
        <th>Output</th>
        <th>Status</th>
      </tr>
